WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.874
Truecell turns difficult PDFs and scans into structured, validated Excel.

2
00:00:03.874 --> 00:00:11.546
It verifies numeric relationships, links every retained value to its source, and records human review from first extraction to final workbook.

3
00:00:11.546 --> 00:00:15.200
Every result arrives with the evidence needed to understand it.

4
00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:19.403
Truecell converts extraction into a complete document intelligence workflow.

5
00:00:19.403 --> 00:00:28.877
It structures complex tables, validates numeric relationships, links cells to their source, guides human review, and packages the full audit trail into the workbook.

6
00:00:28.877 --> 00:00:31.640
Every stage is visible, local, and reproducible.

7
00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:36.981
Truecell runs locally on CPU, without an API key or cloud AI upload.

8
00:00:36.981 --> 00:00:43.476
It handles native PDFs and scanned documents, detects tables automatically, and accepts files up to two hundred pages.

9
00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:49.250
Its included stress suite verifies fifty pages, eight hundred rows, and twelve columns with source traceability.

10
00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:55.118
In this dummy bank statement, the table appears in seconds, but extraction is only step one.

11
00:00:55.118 --> 00:00:57.075
Truecell builds a bounded priority queue.

12
00:00:57.075 --> 00:01:04.250
It flags a wrong total, a sparse summary row, and two running-balance breaks while retaining the original page beside the structured grid.

13
00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:10.672
Selecting the balance finding jumps to row eleven, column Z, and outlines the exact source cell.

14
00:01:10.672 --> 00:01:16.083
The evidence drawer retains the original reading, page, source box, extraction engine, and confidence context.

15
00:01:16.083 --> 00:01:19.690
A reviewer can inspect the document before touching the value.

16
00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:25.313
Truecell discovers repeated numeric relationships instead of relying on fixed financial column names.

17
00:01:25.313 --> 00:01:29.521
Fifteen of seventeen eligible rows agree with the inferred balance equation.

18
00:01:29.521 --> 00:01:32.964
The printed value, one thousand eighty-one, breaks two checks.

19
00:01:32.964 --> 00:01:36.790
Two equation instances support a proposal of one thousand sixty-four.

20
00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:41.020
Before editing, Truecell evaluates the proposal on a disposable copy.

21
00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:46.747
Review findings fall from four to two, and failed equation checks fall from two to zero.

22
00:01:46.747 --> 00:01:48.537
The working data remains unchanged.

23
00:01:48.537 --> 00:01:53.190
Agreement is evidence, not permission, so the agent never silently applies the correction.

24
00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:59.100
After checking the source, the reviewer supplies a reason and explicitly saves the corrected value.

25
00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:05.413
The original reading remains available, and the audit rail records the before value, after value, timestamp, and explanation.

26
00:02:05.413 --> 00:02:08.920
This is a traceable human decision, not an invisible rewrite.

27
00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:15.914
Now the difficult case: five raster-only pages, twelve columns, repeated headers, and records split across page boundaries.

28
00:02:15.914 --> 00:02:22.258
Truecell joins all five pages into one table, removes four repeated headers, and recovers both split rows.

29
00:02:22.258 --> 00:02:25.990
The join receipt exposes every merge instead of hiding it.

30
00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:31.397
This disclosed stress fixture contains fifty pages, eight hundred rows, and twelve columns.

31
00:02:31.397 --> 00:02:34.691
Searching for invoice eight hundred returns one exact match.

32
00:02:34.691 --> 00:02:39.448
Selecting it moves straight to page fifty and outlines the original source value.

33
00:02:39.448 --> 00:02:42.010
Search never breaks the row-to-page evidence link.

34
00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:47.297
Truecell tests its validation layer with controlled edits applied only to disposable copies.

35
00:02:47.297 --> 00:02:54.430
In this run, fourteen of twenty-four changes generated a new finding, while the source data and review history remained untouched.

36
00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:58.710
This turns error detection into a measurable, repeatable workflow with visible results.

37
00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:02.655
The Excel output is designed for action and verification.

38
00:03:02.655 --> 00:03:10.345
Alongside the data, it includes cell evidence, validation findings, the join receipt, page audit, inferred constraints, correction history, verification, and provenance.

39
00:03:10.345 --> 00:03:16.936
Any exported value can be traced back to its original page with the full processing trail beside it.

40
00:03:17.586 --> 00:03:22.323
Across Truecell's disclosed development suite, all twenty-two cases passed their defined exact checks.

41
00:03:22.323 --> 00:03:30.704
The packaged RapidOCR suite passed all five scan cases with Tesseract excluded, and the public Unicode audit matched all one hundred twenty-six cells.

42
00:03:30.704 --> 00:03:35.806
Every result is backed by fixtures, workbooks, and machine-readable reports included with the project.

43
00:03:36.456 --> 00:03:47.593
Truecell turns difficult documents into defensible spreadsheets through one local, end-to-end workflow: extraction, validation, cell-level source evidence, human review, and a complete audit trail.

44
00:03:47.593 --> 00:03:48.985
Built for trust.

45
00:03:48.985 --> 00:03:50.377
Built for scale.

46
00:03:50.377 --> 00:03:50.841
Truecell.

47
00:03:50.841 --> 00:03:52.697
Every cell, accounted for.

